  "notes": "⚠ `low` is the research's own rating (medium-low) and the reason is precise: their identity, era, mentorship under Jim Jonsin and a per-track credit list on Denzel Curry's *Ta13oo* and *Melt My Eyez* are documented, but **every sonic parameter is inference from those records** and marked `[LOW-CONF]`. So all of the below is INFERRED, and what it is inferred *from* is the paragraph's one structural argument: they have \"genuine harmonic motion — the *Ta13oo* material moves between i–VI–III–VII and i–iv–VII with m7/m9 extensions, which is what lets the same producer serve both the 'Light' and 'Dark' acts of that record\". That is why this is a four-chord model with seventh- and ninth-weighted extensions rather than a static-i one. The second inferred claim is a dynamics one, stated as a contrast: \"cleaner and more dynamic than the Ronny J bench — velocity variation on hats and audible room on the clap\". Set against `ronny-j`'s crushed 118–127/110–120/86–98, this file runs 104–124 over 74–92 over 34–50 with hat velocities spanning 0.62–1.0 and `layerClapOffsetMs` at 6–12ms for the room. Third, \"tuned 808 with long portamento glides tracking the chord roots; moderate saturation rather than clipping\" is `glideProb` 0.75 — the highest in this batch — with `distortion` `medium`. Fourth, \"a real countermelody above the hook — higher note density than the rest of this lane\" is `densityRatio` 0.65 at a +12 offset over 5–9 notes a bar on `pluck_synth`. The arrangement is the documented one: melody alone, drums at bar 5, 16-bar verses, 8-bar hooks, mid-song beat switches serving the album's act structure.",
